cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use meltiro in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "meltiro: agentic LLM-assisted data extraction for systematic reviews"
abstract: >-
  meltiro is a pipeline for AI-assisted data extraction and quality assessment
  as part of evidence synthesis studies. It coordinates the agentic construction
  of an extraction output in which fields are linked to figures, tables and
  quotes from the paper wherever possible, and checked by multiple agents with
  differing context. A run takes a paper bundle (clean full text file with cropped
  figures and tables) together with a config bundle (extraction
  template, prompts, reference lists, and pipeline settings), and returns a
  validated extraction output. Each field is deterministically validated against
  the requirements of the extraction template at every stage, with passing fields
  committed to the extraction output and errors returned to the agent with an
  informative error message. Wherever a field is linked to evidence (a quote,
  figure or table) its existence in the paper is deterministically checked, 
  and the interpretation of that evidence is cross-checked by an LLM.
  Three deliberately uncorrelated roles participate: an Extractor, a per-field
  Checker with restricted context, and a Reviewer with a fresh context. The inputs
  for every run generate a fingerprint, meaning while extraction outputs
  are not reproducible, runs with identical inputs and/or configurations can be
  meaningfully compared.
type: software
